A NOTE ON THE CONTENT

The church calendar shown in this application (fasts, feasts, tones,
commemorations and the appointed readings) comes from orthocal.info and its
open-source code. The calendar bundled with the application was generated 
from that code. Any content generated from Orthocal that is not in the public 
domain was replaced with public-domain equivalents.

The scripture is the King James Version with the Apocrypha, which is in the
public domain, from eBible.org. Orthocal's saints' lives, and the Composite
readings whose translation is not in the public domain, are not used. The
passages from the Church Fathers are drawn from translations published between
1885 and 1900, which are in the public domain. The prayers are from older
public-domain liturgical English, chiefly the Hapgood Service Book of 1906.

The daily lives of the saints are the Prologue from Ochrid by St. Nikolai
Velimirovic, from app.ochrid.com, shown unchanged and licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence (CC BY-SA 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Those texts remain under
that licence; it does not extend to the rest of the software.

The glossary and other explanatory text are the author's own and carry the same
terms as the software.

Nothing in this application is authoritative on matters of faith or practice.
It has not been reviewed or approved by any ecclesiastical authority.
